design.cli_and_api:
CLI: a new command, `grade`. estimate is untouched, since agency samples have no sidecar.

oe-inferencex grade POINTS.csv --stratum COL --reference COL --map COL
  [--alternate COL ...]      # agreement when the map gives the primary or any alternate
  [--also-accept FILE]       # per map class, extra reference classes (estimate's _also_accept_pairs format)
  [--other COL]              # a second map at the same points: adds the comparison
  [--crosswalk FILE]         # {column: {code: class}} for map, other, reference, alternates
  (--weight COL | --inclusion COL | --sizes FILE --size-column COL [--size-stratum-column COL] --sizes-are counts|areas [--area-unit ha|km2|m2])
  [--unit-area A]            # areas only: the sampling unit's area, for the deflation; default 1 ha, printed
  [--no-assignment CODES] [--map-nodata CODES] [--unassigned bound|drop]
  [--pure-strata FILE | --strata-are-map-classes]
  [--keep COL=VALUE ...]     # explicit frame filter; rows dropped are counted
  [--classes CODES] [--class-names FILE] [--cells] [--joint] [--level 0.95]
  [--map-date D --other-date D --reference-date D] [--out FILE]

Every option that changes a reading is fixed before labels are read: rules, crosswalks, purity, legend, level and joint.

PRINTED OUTPUT (format only)
- A design header: H, n, range of n_h, size kind, population model, unit area, frame and unknown counts.
- One line per reading, for example:
  "overall accuracy, primary or alternate: X% (finite-sample 95%: A% to B%, stratified betting; normal-theory, nominal: C% to D%)"
  With two readings, a note that they hold together at 90%.
- A per-class table:
  - user's accuracy, with its method named: pure stratum or betting;
  - producer's accuracy;
  - reference area share, and area in ha or km²;
  - map bias;
  - each with its finite-sample and nominal interval.
- The error matrix in area proportions, sum_h W_h n_hij/n_h, with counts and SEs. Also written as CSV. Cell intervals with --cells.
- A comparison block for --other.
- A note: each interval is its own 95% statement (or joint with --joint), finite-sample for every population given the stated weights, and about 1.6× the nominal width beside it.

JSON
- kind "grade"; design "reference sample"; interval_kind "finite-sample"; level; population {kind: counts|areas|weights, unit_area, per stratum n, N or area, W}.
- readings: {primary | primary_or_alternate | also_accept: {...}}. Each reading holds:
  - overall_accuracy: {estimate, finite_sample {low, high, method}, nominal {low, high, se}};
  - error_matrix: {classes, proportions, counts, se, cells?};
  - per_class[c]: {user_accuracy, producer_accuracy, reference_share, area {unit}, map_share, map_bias, n_mapped, n_reference, warning_codes}, each finite_sample plus nominal plus method;
  - comparison: {difference, finite_sample, nominal, verdict, e_value_a, e_value_b}.
- mixture {c_grid, alpha}, joint, unknown {n, rule}, frame {kept, dropped}, notes, written_by.

PYTHON API (numpy only, except reading)
- oe_inferencex.stratified:
  - mean_interval(strata, level=0.95), where strata are [{W, n, N | None, unit_N | None, counts {value: count}}];
  - ratio_interval(strata_yz, level);
  - difference_interval(strata_d, level);
  - pure_stratum_user_accuracy(N, n, W, kA, kB, own, mixed, level, gamma=0.005);
  - normal_mean and normal_ratio (Stehman 2014; must equal estimate._ht_total and _ht_ratio);
  - each interval returns (low, high, info).
- oe_inferencex.agency:
  - read_points(path, stratum=, reference=, map=, alternates=(), other=None, weight= | inclusion= | sizes=, sizes_are=, area_unit=, unit_area=1.0, no_assignment=(), map_nodata=(), keep=None, crosswalk=None, classes=None) returns a ReferenceSample (validated);
  - grade(sample, also_accept=None, pure_strata=None, unassigned="bound", cells=False, joint=False, level=0.95) returns the result dict;
  - compare(sample, ...);
  - summary(result).

order_of_work:
1. Main session: run nothing locally. Copy betting_widths.py, agency_bounds.py, judge/judge_agency.py, judge/judge_job.sh and data/breadth/gfc2020/strata_size.csv into one directory on aicr. Before submitting, state the risks: cpu partition, 16 cores, 16 GB, ≤ 3 h 30 limit, about 1 h expected, a few hundred MB of scratch, one job, no polling. Then run `sbatch judge_job.sh SRC_DIR`. Read the outputs after the mail.

2. Read the gates in order:
   - betting selftest;
   - judge enum, including the uncapped ratio engine;
   - bounds enum;
   - widths checks (sizing.json and record reproduction);
   - Monte Carlo.
   Any false gate stops everything: no width is quoted, and the bug goes back to the script or the construction.

3. Settle the alternate-label rule from table4: which reference-area and producer's-accuracy definition reproduces Table 4. Note the Lalt16L1 gap.

4. Read judge_select's verdict per family. It is fixed by the pre-declared rule. Owner calls that remain:
   - marginal against joint default;
   - "finite-sample" wording;
   - accepting two engines if the verdict is mixed.

5. Implement oe_inferencex/stratified.py: the engine (DP vectorised over c and over strata, warm-started scan, pure-stratum rule, deflation, normal theory). Port the exact tests from the scripts. Run targeted tests locally only if the owner allows; otherwise on the cluster.

6. Implement oe_inferencex/agency.py and cli.cmd_grade: reading, rules, refusals, report, comparison. Add the decide changes (kind "grade", structured interval_kind, difference_within) and the MCP refusal text. Add the CLI golden test and the decide tests.

7. Run the full suite on the cluster (branch cluster-suite) and a self-review. The Codex co-audit step in CLAUDE.md is retired: the memory says no Codex.

8. Make one recorded end-to-end run on the cluster: grade on NLCD set B (2016 and 2011, levels II and I, both readings, against LCMAP) and on GFC2020 (both maps, bounded no-assignment from the agency CSV). It must reproduce the published OA and Table 4 within rounding. Then an independent audit; then claims.yaml entries; then scripts/claims.py stale.

9. Docs: Usage section, README row and guarantee bullet, CHANGELOG. Release 1.18.0 after CI is green, and verify on PyPI.

10. Later, each its own decision:
   - an MCP grade tool after an agent pilot;
   - raster extraction and DBF reading;
   - plan for agency designs;
   - an anytime variant;
   - porting the engine to estimate's condition and class designs after grading on exp116's maps.
